    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11250" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cŏrōnis</span></b> ,
			ĭdis, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κορωνίς</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>daughter of the Thessalian Phlegyas,
				mother of Æsculapius by Apollo</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 2,
				542</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab. 161</span></i> and 202;
					<i><span class="en">Serv. ad Verg. A. 6, 618</span></i>;
				acc. Gr. Coronida, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 2,
				599</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cŏrōnīdes</span></b> ,
			ae, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κορωνείδης</span>, <i>the son of
			Coronis</i>, i. e. <i>Æsculapius</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 15,
				624</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
